  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving health interventions in flood affected districts in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The key objective of this project is to improve Lifesaving health interventions in flood-affected districts in Rwanda. This WHO project provides lifesaving medicine and essential medical equipment, epidemiological surveillance and laboratory services, distribution of dignity kits and emergency Reproductive Health kits, and maternal health and Sexual Reproductive Health equipment and material in total, the project targets 18,854 people, including 5,970 women, 3,243 men, and 9,641 children 498 persons with disabilities are also supported.</narrative>
  </description>
